<odoo>
    <!--
        The paper the Registrar issues, and the paper it demands.

        Three validity models are in use here and the distinction is the whole
        reason legal.document.type has a validity_model at all:

        * A certificate of incorporation never expires. It is superseded when the
          company is amended, but it does not lapse - validity_model = 'none'.
        * A certified lease or an expediter's authorisation expires on a date -
          validity_model = 'expiry'.
        * A paid electricity bill never expires and yet is refused the moment it
          is old. Council of Ministers directive 16180 of 1 April 2024 made the
          LATEST paid electricity and water bills mandatory attachments at the
          Registrar, and the Ministry of Planning refuses any supporting letter
          issued more than a year before the application. Both are
          validity_model = 'freshness', and an expiry date could not express
          either of them.
    -->
